WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.390
Writer/director James Gunn's upcoming soft
reboot The Suicide Squad will likely be missing

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.760
the original's most divisive element.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.080
In a recent Q&amp;A conducted on Instagram, Gunn
appeared to shoot down the idea of Jared Leto's

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.140
Joker appearing in his film in response to
a question from a fan.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.140
Gunn was asked:

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.400
"How can you justify a Suicide Squad movie
that does not have Joker in it?"

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.880
Gunn's response was simple:

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.490
"No one but me and a few others know all the
characters in the movie, but if the Joker

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:32.090
isn't in the film, I don't think it would
be strange as he isn't a part of the Suicide

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.719
Squad in the comics."

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:38.229
Gunn's absolutely correct that Joker isn't
a part of the Suicide Squad in the comics,

00:00:38.229 --> 00:00:42.579
which is one reason why some fans were puzzled
at the character's inclusion in the original

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:44.550
2016 film in the first place.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.519
The version of the Clown Prince of Crime presented
in director David Ayer's Suicide Squad was

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:54.409
just a bit different from the cinematic depictions
of the past, and most DC die-hards agreed

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:56.030
that it was not in a good way.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.870
Leto's Joker's pasty white face and slicked-back,
bright green hair were about the only facets

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.899
of the character's physical appearance that
the flick got right.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:09.580
The platinum grill and tattoos looked absurd
to many fans, and Leto's hyper-stylized, weirdly

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.450
off-putting performance did little to quell
their anger when it hit theaters.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:18.490
"I am not someone who is loved.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.650
I'm an idea.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.560
A state of mind."

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.840
Gunn's principal cast for The Suicide Squad
could already fill a good-sized bus.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.960
The cast was revealed last month with the
release of a one-sheet that included a whopping

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.590
24 names, featuring both new and returning
cast members.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.570
At this late juncture, it seems pretty unlikely
that Gunn will sneak Leto into the film, and

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.730
this latest comment all but confirms the fact
that The Suicide Squad will leave the actor's

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.780
version of the Joker out in the cold.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.590
Despite the extremely mixed reception to Leto's
Joker, Suicide Squad made enough bank that

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.420
a solo vehicle for the character and a team-up
with Margot Robbie's Harley Quinn were briefly

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.909
put into development.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:01.800
Both of those projects, however, were unceremoniously
axed earlier this year - and that's not even

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.060
the strongest indication that Warner Brothers
has completely soured on Leto's version of

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.060
the Joker.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.670
Let's not forget that the trailer for the
upcoming Birds of Prey film makes it clear

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:16.000
that, especially as far as Harley Quinn is
concerned, "Mr. J" is out of the picture.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.550
There's also the fact that the standalone,
Joaquin Phoenix -starring Joker movie made

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.310
absurd amounts of money, and seems to have
practically guaranteed its star a Best Actor

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.310
Oscar nomination.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.819
While it's pretty safe to say that Phoenix's
Joker is going to remain strictly its own

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:33.519
thing, that doesn't mean that Leto was thrilled
about the new film.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.060
Recent reports have indicated that the actor
felt both alienated and upset by the fact

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.560
that the movie was even put into development.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.550
Joker's ridiculous success and domination
of the pop culture conversation this fall

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:48.249
probably haven't made Leto feel any better
about the whole thing.

00:02:48.249 --> 00:02:52.450
At this point, it's not clear that Leto would
return to the role even if he were asked.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.840
In the meantime, he'll appear as the titular
Living Vampire in next year's Morbius from

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.969
Sony and Marvel.

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:02.919
If that film even approaches the box office
heights of Venom, then the Morbius gig could

00:03:02.919 --> 00:03:04.779
become a recurring one for Leto.

00:03:04.779 --> 00:03:08.870
If Sony and Marvel Studios continue to play
as nice as they have been in the last month

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.889
or so, he could even find himself facing off
with Tom Holland's wildly popular Spider-Man.

00:03:13.889 --> 00:03:18.019
In any event, it's beginning to look more
and more like Leto's Joker will end up as

00:03:18.019 --> 00:03:21.290
a one-and-done, which will suit most fans
just fine.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.950
The Suicide Squad hits the big screen in August,
2021.

